viogpu3d: 32-bit (WOW64) user-mode drivers, and a safe capset copy

Applies to max8rr8/kvm-guest-drivers-windows@viogpu3d (9ed3aab), together with Mesa patch 0002.

- VIOGPU_CAPSET_REQ carried a raw pointer, so a 32-bit process sent a different layout. Make it a UINT64 on both
  sides.
- The capset escape copied into that user-supplied address without probing it, letting any process that can open
  the adapter make the kernel write to kernel memory. ProbeForWrite it first.
- Package and register 32-bit builds of the Mesa user-mode drivers (UserModeDriverNameWow, OpenGLDriverNameWow).
  Without them 32-bit apps get no D3D10/11 at all (DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED) and only software OpenGL 1.1.
- Drop z.dll from the package: Mesa now links zlib statically.

diff --git a/viogpu/shared/viogpum.h b/viogpu/shared/viogpum.h
index 51810d3..d4756e9 100644
--- a/viogpu/shared/viogpum.h
+++ b/viogpu/shared/viogpum.h
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ typedef struct _VIOGPU_CAPSET_REQ
     ULONG CapsetId;
     ULONG Version;
     ULONG Size;
-    UCHAR *Capset;
+    UINT64 Capset; // user-mode buffer address; 64 bits wide so 32-bit (WOW64) callers use the same layout
 } VIOGPU_CAPSET_REQ;
 #pragma pack()
 
